			"name": "01 - Authentification",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Token CLIENT",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Token HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('clientToken', pm.response.json().access_token);"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{
									"key": "grant_type",
									"value": "password",
									"type": "text"
								},
								{
									"key": "client_id",
									"value": "{{clientId}}",
									"type": "text"
								},
								{
									"key": "username",
									"value": "{{clientUsername}}",
									"type": "text"
								},
								{
									"key": "password",
									"value": "{{clientPassword}}",
									"type": "text"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
							"host": [
								"{{keycloakUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"realms",
								"{{realm}}",
								"protocol",
								"openid-connect",
								"token"
							]
						},
						"description": "## Endpoint Description\n\nThis endpoint is used to obtain an access token from the Keycloak server for authentication and authorization purposes. It is part of the OpenID Connect protocol and is typically used in scenarios where a client application needs to authenticate a user and receive tokens for accessing protected resources.\n\n### Request\n\n**Method:** POST  \n**URL:** `{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token`  \n**Content-Type:** `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`\n\n#### Expected Input Parameters\n\nThe request body must be formatted as `x-www-form-urlencoded`. The specific parameters required may vary based on the authentication flow being used (e.g., password grant, client credentials). Common parameters include:\n\n- `grant_type`: The type of grant being requested (e.g., `password`, `client_credentials`).\n    \n- `client_id`: The ID of the client making the request.\n    \n- `client_secret`: The secret of the client (if applicable).\n    \n- `username`: The username of the user (if applicable).\n    \n- `password`: The password of the user (if applicable).\n    \n\nNote: The actual parameters used in the last call are not provided.\n\n### Response\n\n**Status Code:** 200  \n**Content-Type:** `application/json`\n\n#### Response Structure\n\nOn a successful request, the response will contain the following fields:\n\n- `access_token`: The token that can be used to authenticate requests to protected resources.\n    \n- `expires_in`: The duration in seconds for which the access token is valid.\n    \n- `refresh_expires_in`: The duration in seconds for which the refresh token is valid.\n    \n- `refresh_token`: A token that can be used to obtain a new access token when the current one expires.\n    \n- `token_type`: The type of token issued (typically \"Bearer\").\n    \n- `not-before-policy`: The time before which the token is not valid.\n    \n- `session_state`: The state of the user's session.\n    \n- `scope`: The scopes associated with the access token.\n    \n\nThis endpoint is essential for obtaining tokens required for secure communication between client applications and the Keycloak server."
					},
					"response": []
				},
